        "uncertainties_disclosed": false
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "διὸ πρὸς τοὺς σώζειν αὐτοὺς δυναμένους ἐλθεῖν ὀκνηρότεροι γίνονται καὶ τοὺς ὑπ’ αὐτῶν τῶν ἐνεδρευόντων δαιμόνων ἀναλισκόμενοι ἀγνοοῦσιν.",
          "english_quote": "Therefore they become more reluctant to go to those capable of saving them, and, while being consumed by the very demons lying in wait for them, they remain unaware.",
          "issue": "The English supplies no object for ἀγνοοῦσιν and no English value for the surviving accusative τοὺς. The source note assumes that τοὺς should agree with ἀναλισκόμενοι, but it can instead be considered an anaphoric accusative object of ἀγνοοῦσιν, referring back to those capable of saving them. On that reading, the nominative participle describes the people who fail to recognize those helpers. The note's proposed deletion therefore does not establish fidelity to the supplied reading. This problem is separate from the four-dot lacuna, which the draft faithfully represents and discloses.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider: “Therefore they become more reluctant to go to those capable of saving them, and, while being consumed by the very demons lying in wait for them, they fail to recognize them.” Explain that the final “them” takes τοὺς anaphorically as referring to those capable of saving them, and preserve any viable referent alternatives. Revise the source note so that it does not present agreement with the participle as obligatory. This candidate requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "reference": "9.13",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": false,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "lexical_fidelity": false,
        "uncertainties_disclosed": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ εἰς τέλος κολασθησομένας καθιστᾶσιν τῶν ἀνακεκραμένων τὰς ἠπατημένας αὐτοῖς ψυχάς",
          "english_quote": "they put the deceived souls of those who have been mingled with them in a state of being punished to the end",
          "issue": "κολασθησομένας is a future passive participle: the souls will undergo punishment. “In a state of being punished” instead presents punishment as an already operative state. The lexical note discusses the extent expressed by εἰς τέλος but does not address this loss of prospective force.",
          "suggested_revision": "Replace the quoted phrase with a prospective formulation, such as “they bring it about that the deceived souls of those who have been mingled with them will be punished to the end.” Retain the disclosed alternatives concerning the extent of εἰς τέλος and the subject of χωρήσαντες. The revised wording requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "reference": "9.14",
      "verdict": "accept",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": true,
        "names_and_negations": true,
